   [woodhams@phoenix.Princeton.EDU (Michael Woodhams) writes:]
   [] I'm surprised no one has suggested the obvious solution - instead of
   [] producing a random item if you wish for something non-existant, why not
   [] just say "that item does not exist. Please try again." ...

   currently in 3.0 wishing is like that. you get 5 chances (i think) to
   ask for a misspelled wish correctly before the game gives you an
   appropriate prize to terminate the interaction. that's not really at
   issue ...

Yes it is.
The trouble is that is is done only to general item class like armor.
Why couldn't this be done so that every word in wish is checked like
blessed +3 dragon scale mail
blessed understood
+3 understood
dragon not understood (should be like gray dragon)
scale mail understood

I think this would be reasonably programmable also.

